name: sim.alignShapeBB
description: Reorients the bounding box of a shape, while keeping the shape frame in place. The shape's inertia properties are unaffected
luaSynopsis: bool result = sim.alignShapeBB(int shapeHandle, list pose)
pythonSynopsis: bool result = sim.alignShapeBB(int shapeHandle, float[7] pose)
inputs:
1. shapeHandle: handle of the shape
2. pose: pose describing the new orientation of the shape's bounding box. The pose is expressed as [x y z qx qy qz qw], where the positional part is ignored. A pose containing only zeros aligns the bounding box with the mesh's natural bounding box
outputs:
1. result: 0 if the bounding box could not be reoriented (the bounding box of primitive shapes cannot be reoriented), otherwise 1.
